## CR-03 — STILL LIVE + CONSTITUTIONAL

- `apps/worker/src/jobs/email-delivery.ts:95` — `const nodeEnv = deps.nodeEnv ?? process.env.NODE_ENV;` (LOCKER-01 hit).
- `:111` — `if (result.reason === "smtp-not-configured" && nodeEnv !== "production") { return; }` (silent-green carve-out).
- `tools/lint-no-env-branches.allowlist.txt:30` — `apps/worker/src/jobs/email-delivery.ts:80  # issue-31-DI-fallback-jsdoc`
- `tools/lint-no-env-branches.allowlist.txt:31` — `apps/worker/src/jobs/email-delivery.ts:95  # issue-31-DI-fallback`
- Phase 61 cross-check: `packages/email/src/EmailSender.ts:109-112` emits `{ delivered: false, reason: "smtp-not-configured" }` — that package read is a separate, correctly-bounded surface; the worker-side carve-out was NOT swept by R19. Confirmed still live.

DECISION (CR-03): boundary file = `apps/worker/src/config/worker-config.ts` (a `*config*.ts` file inside the LOCKER-01 allowed boundary set). It reads `process.env.EMAIL_FALLBACK_NONFATAL` (a real opt-in flag, `"1"`/`"true"` => true) and NOT `NODE_ENV`. The flag is threaded through `index.ts` and injected as `deps.allowSmtpFallback: boolean`. The `smtp-not-configured` path FAILS the job (throws) unless the explicit flag is set.

## CR-04 — STILL LIVE

- `apps/worker/src/lib/with-tenant-context.ts:149-152` — bare `await client.query("ROLLBACK")` inside `catch (handlerErr)`; a throwing ROLLBACK replaces `handlerErr`.

## CR-05 — STILL LIVE

- `apps/worker/src/jobs/partman-maintenance.ts:76-78` — unguarded `for (const partition of detached) await deps.auditArchiveQueue.add(...)`; no per-iteration guard.

DECISION (CR-05): mitigation shape = collect-failures-and-re-throw-after-loop. Rationale: simplest, retry-safe — BullMQ retries the WHOLE detached list; `discoverDetached` is idempotent (already-archived partitions no longer match the predicate) so re-enqueuing on retry is harmless. `Promise.allSettled` would also work but the sequential collect keeps the existing per-iteration ordering and is no harder to read.

## CR-06 — STILL LIVE (worker-local, NOT a wire change)

- `apps/worker/src/jobs/reconciliation-daily-check.ts:231-237` — `discrepancyQueue.add("reconciliation-discrepancy", {...})` with NO `jobId` options arg.
- `apps/worker/src/jobs/reconciliation-discrepancy.ts:28-36` — `reconciliationDiscrepancySchema` is `.object({...}).strict()`, defined LOCAL to `apps/worker`, NOT in `@openwhispr/wire-schemas`. No external suite to run.
- `apps/worker/src/lib/typed-queue.ts:29-33` — `TypedQueue.add` ALREADY forwards an optional `jobsOpts?: JobsOptions` 3rd arg to BullMQ `queue.add`. No widening of `add` required.

DECISION (CR-06): add `window_id: z.string().optional()` additively to the strict schema; pass `{ jobId: \`recon-disc:${window_id}:${tenantId}\` }` as the 3rd arg to `discrepancyQueue.add`. Deterministic `window_id = \`${windowStart}:${windowEnd}\``.

